From 1bf93e4525b98374ad820abaed348f4ebaa9b4e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: znyrvalt <220587351+znyrvalt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 07:43:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] crossplay: honour Blockbench texture_size when sampling
 UVs

The first icons sampled face UVs on a hardcoded 16x16 basis, which is wrong
whenever a Blockbench export lays its uvs out on its declared texture_size
grid, and the icons themselves exposed two deeper sampling defects. All three
are fixed here, with the conventions decided once in javapack and shared by
the renderer and the geometry converter:

- uv_basis(): the honoured basis is data-driven, never assumed. Exports whose
  face uvs reach past the 16-grid are texture-size-grid exports and divide by
  their declared texture_size; exports on the vanilla grid (this pack: uv
  range 0..16 exactly, declared sizes 16/32/64) keep the vanilla scheme,
  because texture_size is Blockbench-only metadata there (minecraft.wiki,
  'Model': fields used by Blockbench, not used by Minecraft). Dividing this
  pack's models by their texture_size would sample the top-left fraction of
  each sheet - warden_heart and dragon_heart land wholly on transparent
  texels that way, which is what scrambled the first cut.
- v axis: the pack's UVs are authored image-space (v from the top scanline);
  the flip the first cut guessed sent every sample into mirrored/transparent
  rows. Decided against a controlled single-quad render of a known 16x16
  texture: direct v reproduces the sprite upright.
- face corners: quad corners are paired with uv corners per face (the
  convention Minecraft's FaceBakery applies, with its winding fix-up), so
  west/east/up/down sample in their true directions instead of mirrored.
- backface culling: the orthographic gui view sees a box's outward faces from
  one side only; drawing the far side mirrored over the near side is what
  garbled everything past the first quad. Quads with non-positive screen
  winding are now culled, which also skips degenerates.
- geometry faces emit the min-based rect under the same honoured basis, so
  the Bedrock side and the icons agree; reversed (mirrored) source rects
  normalise, a documented approximation of Bedrock's rotation-less face UVs.

Validator: check 28 rebuilds every face rect from the raw model + the
honoured basis and must reproduce the shipped geometry exactly; the atlas
bounds check (27) keeps guarding containment. 29 checks, 0 failed.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
